      <p><strong>How much does a tiny house cost?</strong> Most finished tiny houses cost between <strong>$36,000 and $112,000</strong> on a trailer, and roughly <strong>$80,000 to $200,000+</strong> on a permanent foundation, before land. The biggest swing is labor: owner-built tiny houses typically run <strong>$150&ndash;$330 per square foot</strong>, while builder-made homes run <strong>$250&ndash;$500 per square foot</strong>. Land, utilities and permits can add anywhere from a few thousand dollars to as much again as the house itself.</p>
      <p>Those numbers come from the same cost model behind our <a href="/tools/tiny-house-cost-calculator/">tiny house cost calculator</a>. Below, we break them down the way a builder would: by build path, by component and by the line items buyers forget.</p>

