      <h2 id="price-by-path">Tiny house price by build path</h2>
      <p>The same 200 sq ft floor plan can cost $40,000 or $110,000 depending on who builds it and how far they take it. These are the five common routes, with typical all-in ranges for the house itself (land and utility service not included).</p>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Build path</th><th>Typical size</th><th class="num">Typical cost</th><th>What you get</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>DIY tiny house on wheels</td><td>160&ndash;240 sq ft</td><td class="num">$36k &ndash; $78k</td><td>You build everything; licensed trades for electrical and plumbing where required</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Builder shell + DIY finish</td><td>160&ndash;240 sq ft</td><td class="num">$45k &ndash; $85k</td><td>Framed, sheathed, roofed and dried-in shell; you do insulation, systems and interior</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Prebuilt (turnkey) on wheels</td><td>160&ndash;280 sq ft</td><td class="num">$56k &ndash; $112k</td><td>Move-in ready from a builder's standard model line, often RV-certified</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Custom builder on wheels</td><td>200&ndash;340 sq ft</td><td class="num">$90k &ndash; $175k</td><td>One-off design, premium finishes, larger trailers, off-grid packages</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Foundation tiny home</td><td>300&ndash;700 sq ft</td><td class="num">$80k &ndash; $200k+</td><td>Permitted house on piers or slab; can be owner-built or builder-built</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3 id="diy">DIY tiny house cost</h3>
      <p>A DIY tiny house is the cheapest way in, because labor is often 40&ndash;60% of a builder's price. Owner-builders typically spend <strong>$150&ndash;$220 per sq ft</strong> for basic finishes, <strong>$190&ndash;$260</strong> for mid-range and <strong>$240&ndash;$330</strong> for high-end, plus the trailer. The catch is time: plan on 6 to 18 months of evenings and weekends, and budget for tools if you are starting from scratch. Our <a href="/blog/how-to-build-a-tiny-house/">how to build a tiny house</a> guide walks through the 12 stages.</p>

      <h3 id="shell">Shell tiny house cost</h3>
      <p>A shell gets you past the steepest learning curve, the trailer attachment, framing, roof and weather barrier, so you can finish inside at your own pace. Shells commonly run $30k&ndash;$55k depending on size and window package, and finishing them yourself typically adds $15k&ndash;$30k. Ask exactly where the shell stops: some include windows and exterior door, some include rough electrical, some do not include siding.</p>

      <h3 id="builder">Builder and custom tiny house prices</h3>
      <p>Professional builders typically charge <strong>$250&ndash;$330 per sq ft</strong> for basic finishes, <strong>$300&ndash;$400</strong> for mid-range and <strong>$380&ndash;$500</strong> for high-end, plus the trailer. Custom builds with full off-grid packages, hardwood interiors or 10 ft wide trailers that need oversize permits to move go past that. Delivery is usually extra.</p>

      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Run your own numbers</strong>
